ags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#file-upload","content":"File Upload"},"353":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-6","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#drop-target-label","content":"Drop Target Label"},"354":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-7","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#replace-existing-file","content":"Replace Existing File"},"355":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-8","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"356":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-9","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Keyboard"},"357":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-10","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"Screen readers"},"358":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-11","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"359":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-12","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#props","content":"Props"},"360":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-13","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#default","content":"A minimal drop zone. The \\`onDrop\\` callback receives the dropped items; use the exported \\`isFileDropItem\\` guard to narrow them to files. Wrap the instructional text in \\`\\<Text slot=\"label\">\\` so it labels the visually hidden drop button for screen readers."},"361":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-14","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#disabled","content":"Set \\`isDisabled\\` to prevent the drop zone from accepting interactions. The zone is dimmed and the cursor indicates it is not interactive."},"362":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-15","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#file-upload","content":"A reference composition combining \\`DropZone\\` with \\`FileTrigger\\` to support both click-to-browse and drag-and-drop. Use this as a starting point and adapt the accepted formats, size limit, and handlers to your product's requirements."},"363":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-16","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#drop-target-label","content":"Pass a render-prop function as \\`children\\` to change the zone's content while a valid drag is active. Branching on \\`isDropTarget\\` requires no extra state. Pair it with \\`getDropOperation\\` to reject unsupported types - the label only appears when the drag is accepted."},"364":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-17","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#replace-existing-file","content":"Use \\`children\\` as a render function to show different content based on the current zone state - here, swapping the default label for \"Drop to replace\" when a file is already selected and a new drag is active. The same \\`onDrop\\` handler services both the drag path and the \\`FileTrigger\\` click path, so either gesture replaces the selection."},"365":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-18","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Key"},"366":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-19","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Description"},"367":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-20","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"`Tab`"},"368":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-21","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Moves focus to the drop zone"},"369":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-22","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"`Enter` / `Space`"},"370":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-23","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Opens the file picker so files can be selected without a pointer"},"371":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-24","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"The drop zone renders a visually hidden `<button>` inside the container. Assistive technology discovers and announces this button as an interactive element — activating it opens the native file picker without a pointer."},"372":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-25","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"The button's accessible name is built from two sources, combined in order:"},"373":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-26","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"**`<Text slot=\"label\">`** — any `Text` child with `slot=\"label\"` has its `id` linked to the button via `aria-labelledby`. This is the recommended way to provide a contextual label that is also visible to sighted users."},"374":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-27","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"**`aria-label`** — pass `aria-label` on the `DropZone` component to override or supplement the label (e.g. `aria-label=\"Upload profile photo\"`). When no `Text slot=\"label\"` is present and no `aria-label` is set, the button falls back to the default \"DropZone\" label provided by React Aria."},"375":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-28","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Use the drop zone alongside a button-based file picker — drag-and-drop is a convenience, never the only way to upload."},"376":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-29","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Replace the default text with `children` to communicate the accepted file types and size limits up front."},"377":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-30","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Let the drop zone fill its container; constrain it with the surrounding layout rather than setting a fixed width on the component itself."},"378":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-31","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Reflect upload state (validating, uploading, error) outside the drop zone so the target area stays clear and predictable."},"379":{"id":"/docs/components/field","page_id":"/docs/components/field","type":"page","content":"Field primitives","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field"},"380":{"id":"/docs/components/field-0","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field","content":"Composable primitives (Field, FieldLabel, FieldGroup, FieldError) for building form fields"},"381":{"id":"/docs/components/field-1","page_id":"/docs/components/field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field#usage","content":"Usage"},"382":{"id":"/docs/components/field-2","page_id":"/docs/components/field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field#composition","content":"Composition"},"383":{"id":"/docs/components/field-3","page_id":"/docs/components/field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field#positioning-controls-inside-the-group","content":"Positioning controls inside the group"},"384":{"id":"/docs/components/field-4","page_id":"/docs/components/field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field#states","content":"States"},"385":{"id":"/docs/components/field-5","page_id":"/docs/components/field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field#examples","content":"Examples"},"386":{"id":"/docs/components/field-6","page_id":"/docs/components/field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field#default","content":"Default"},"387":{"id":"/docs/components/field-7","page_id":"/docs/components/field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field#leading-control","content":"Leading control"},"388":{"id":"/docs/components/field-8","page_id":"/docs/components/field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field#trailing-control","content":"Trailing control"},"389":{"id":"/docs/components/field-9","page_id":"/docs/components/field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field#icon-accessories","content":"Icon accessories"},"390":{"id":"/docs/components/field-10","page_id":"/docs/components/field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field#props","content":"Props"},"391":{"id":"/docs/components/field-11","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field","content":"**Composition primitives.** The field components (TextField, NumberField, DateField, Select, RadioGroup, CheckboxGroup) compose these internally — reach for those first. These primitives are also the building blocks for custom composite fields, e.g. an input and a select sharing one bordered box."},"392":{"id":"/docs/components/field-12","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field","content":"The field decoration is split into granular, composable pieces so the same structure is shared across every field:"},"393":{"id":"/docs/components/field-13","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field","content":"**`Field`** — stacks a field's label, control, description, and error in one consistently spaced column (pure layout — a `Flex` column with the standard field gap)."},"394":{"id":"/docs/components/field-14","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field","content":"**`FieldLabel`** — names the field and flags whether it's required (wraps React Aria `Label`, rendering an optional `*` indicator)."},"395":{"id":"/docs/components/field-15","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field","content":"**`FieldGroup`** — the bordered box that visually unites a field's controls and reflects their shared focus, disabled, and invalid state. Used only by \"boxed\" fields (TextField, NumberField, Select, DateField); presentationally it is a React Aria `Group`."},"396":{"id":"/docs/components/field-16","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field","content":"**`FieldInput`** — the single-line control the user types into (a normalized React Aria `Input` given antares spacing via `Box`)."},"397":{"id":"/docs/components/field-17","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field","content":"**`FieldTextArea`** — the multiline control the user types into (a normalized React Aria `TextArea` given antares spacing via `Box`)."},"398":{"id":"/docs/components/field-18","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field","content":"**`FieldButton`** — an actionable control placed inside the box, such as the NumberField steppers or a search submit (a click target within the group)."},"399":{"id":"/docs/components/field-19","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field","content":"**`FieldTrigger`** — a full-width value-display button inside the box that opens an overlay (used by Select and DatePicker): a value area plus a trailing icon, laid out across the group. `variant=\"select\"` is transparent and input-like; `variant=\"control\"` is a filled segment inside a shared group."},"400":{"id":"/docs/components/field-20","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field","content":"**`FieldDescription`** — helper text that explains the field; renders nothing when empty (wraps the antares `Text` with `slot=\"description\"`)."},"401":{"id":"/docs/components/field-21","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field","content":"**`FieldError`** — surfaces the field's validation messages when it is invalid, and nothing when valid (a thin wrapper over React Aria `FieldError`)."},"402":{"id":"/docs/components/field-22","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field","content":"`FieldLabel`, `FieldDescription`, and `FieldError` each render `null` when they have no content, so callers pass `label` / `description` / `errorMessage` straight through without guarding."},"403":{"id":"/docs/components/field-23","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#composition","content":"A boxed field composes the primitives inside its React Aria field wrapper. Use\n`Field as={...}` to merge the field wrapper and the layout column into a single\nelement:"},"404":{"id":"/docs/components/field-24","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#composition","content":"A field without a box (RadioGroup / CheckboxGroup) composes `Field` + `FieldLabel` + `FieldError` and omits `FieldGroup`."},"405":{"id":"/docs/components/field-25","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#composition","content":"`FieldGroup` is purely presentational — it renders the styled `Group` and holds no React Aria context. The surrounding field wires value, disabled, and validation state into its controls."},"406":{"id":"/docs/components/field-26","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#positioning-controls-inside-the-group","content":"`FieldGroup` rounds its outer corners from DOM order: the group's CSS rounds the start corners of its **first child** and the end corners of its **last child**, so controls are seamless inside and rounded only at the box edges. Author children in visual order and the rounding follows — no per-control positioning prop. A lone control (a TextField input, a Select trigger) is both first and last, so it rounds both edges. The rules are RTL-safe (they use logical `start`/`end` corners)."},"407":{"id":"/docs/components/field-27","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#states","content":"The states **disabled**, **readonly**, and **invalid** are applied by the field wrapper (e.g. TextField, NumberField, Select). The group reflects them via data attributes on the group."},"408":{"id":"/docs/components/field-28","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#states","content":"State"},"409":{"id":"/docs/components/field-29","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#states","content":"CSS Selector"},"410":{"id":"/docs/components/field-30","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#states","content":"disabled — Applied when the field wrapper is disabled."},"411":{"id":"/docs/components/field-31","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#states","content":"`[data-disabled]`"},"412":{"id":"/docs/components/field-32","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#states","content":"invalid — Applied when the field wrapper is invalid (e.g. validation failed)."},"413":{"id":"/docs/components/field-33","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#states","content":"`[data-invalid]`"},"414":{"id":"/docs/components/field-34","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#states","content":"focus — Whether an element within the group has keyboard focus (for focus-ring styling)."},"415":{"id":"/docs/components/field-35","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#states","content":"`[data-focused]`"},"416":{"id":"/docs/components/field-36","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#default","content":"Composes the presentational field primitives (Field, FieldLabel, FieldGroup,\nFieldDescription) into a minimal boxed field, showing how the group and its\nposition markers are assembled. The fill is a static placeholder - real value,\nfocus, and validation behavior is wired up by the field components (TextField,\nNumberField, Select)."},"417":{"id":"/docs/components/field-37","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#leading-control","content":"A field group with a leading control before the input area."},"418":{"id":"/docs/components/field-38","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#trailing-control","content":"A field group with an input and a trailing action control."},"419":{"id":"/docs/components/field-39","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#icon-accessories","content":"A field group with leading icon and trailing action accessories."},"420":{"id":"/docs/components/field-40","page_id":"/docs/components/field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field#props","content":"The `FieldGroup` component has the following props:"},"421":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"page","content":"FileTrigger","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger"},"422":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-0","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger","content":"A style-less primitive that wraps any pressable component and opens the native file picker when it is activated."},"423":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-1","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#features","content":"Features"},"424":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-2","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#installation","content":"Installation"},"425":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-3","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#examples","content":"Examples"},"426":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-4","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#default","content":"Default"},"427":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-5","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#accepted-types","content":"Accepted Types"},"428":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-6","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"429":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-7","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"430":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-8","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#props","content":"Props"},"431":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-9","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#features","content":"Turns any pressable component (such as an Antares `Button`) into a file picker trigger."},"432":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-10","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#features","content":"Renders a visually hidden `<input type=\"file\">` — no styling of its own."},"433":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-11","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#features","content":"Restricts selection by MIME type, allows multiple files, directory selection, and camera capture."},"434":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-12","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#features","content":"Resets the input value before every open, so re-selecting the same file still fires `onSelect`."},"435":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-13","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#default","content":"Wrap any pressable component. Activating the child opens the native file picker; the selected files arrive in \\`onSelect\\`."},"436":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-14","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#accepted-types","content":"Restrict the picker to specific MIME types with \\`acceptedFileTypes\\`, and allow more than one file with \\`allowsMultiple\\`."},"437":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-15","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#accessibility","content":"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."},"438":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-16","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#best-practices","content":"`acceptedFileTypes` is a best-effort filter for the OS picker — always validate file type and size again in your `onSelect` handler, since it can be bypassed."},"439":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-17","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#best-practices","content":"Pair `FileTrigger` with `DropZone` to offer both click-to-browse and drag-and-drop. See the DropZone \"File Upload\" example."},"440":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-18","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#best-practices","content":"Keep the child a single pressable element; `FileTrigger` forwards press behavior to whatever you nest inside it."},"441":{"id":"/docs/components/icon","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","type":"page","content":"Icon","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/icon"},"442":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-0","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/icon","content":"Flexible SVG icon component with on-demand loading, automatic caching, and extensive customization options"},"443":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-1","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/icon#features","content":"Features"},"444":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-2","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/icon#installation","content":"Installation"},"445":{"id":"/docs