s/layout/flex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/flex","content":"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."},"1505":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/flex-16","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/flex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/flex","content":"**Recommended default**: Use `Flex` for most layouts. Since it extends `Box`, you get all `Box` capabilities without needing to nest components."},"1506":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/flex-17","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/flex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/flex#scale-sizes","content":"We use the same scale sizes as the `Box` component. For more information, see the **Box component documentation**."},"1507":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/flex-18","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/flex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/flex#default","content":"Basic horizontal flex layout with gap."},"1508":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/flex-19","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/flex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/flex#direction","content":"The \\`direction\\` prop controls the main axis orientation."},"1509":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/flex-20","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/flex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/flex#alignment","content":"Use \\`justifyContent\\` for main-axis distribution and \\`alignItems\\` for cross-axis alignment."},"1510":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/flex-21","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/flex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/flex#gap","content":"The \\`gap\\` prop controls spacing between children. Use \\`rowGap\\` and \\`columnGap\\` for independent control."},"1511":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/flex-22","page_id":"/docs/compon