er. Assistive technology discovers and announces this button as an interactive element — activating it opens the native file picker without a pointer."],[1481,"The elevation prop adds visual depth using box-shadow."],[392,"The field decoration is split into granular, composable pieces so the same structure is shared across every field:"],[503,"The following methods are exported from `@godaddy/antares` for custom icon management:"],[1186,"The group follows the document's layout direction, detected automatically from the browser locale."],[140,"The hide controls carousel is a carousel that hides the navigation controls."],[496,"The Icon component uses Bento's slot system with the following component hierarchy and available slot override points:"],[675,"The info trigger button uses `aria-label=\"More information\"` to describe its purpose."],[677,"The info trigger has a minimum touch target of 44×44px, achieved via a CSS pseudo-element, to meet WCAG 2.5.5."],[80,"The inline button sits within a run of text, styled like a link while retaining button semantics."],[744,"The input is associated with the visible label and optional description and error content for assistive technologies."],[621,"The ListBox component accepts the following props:"],[654,"The MetricsLockup component displays a single metric with an optional title, info tooltip, trend indicator, and description."],[81,"The minimal button is an icon-only button that's used when space is limited and/or when the action is universally understood."],[683,"The Modal component presents a dialog window over the page that focuses the user's attention on a single task or piece of information."],[1480,"The padding props support t-shirt sizes and CSS logical properties for RTL support."],[768,"The Popover component is an overlay element positioned relative to a trigger element."],[73,"The primary button should be used to indicate the most important action for the user to take in their current experience."],[1482,"The rounding prop sets border-radius. Use \\`full\\` for fully rounded corners."],[74,"The secondary button indicates an action of secondary importance."],[937,"The segmented controller follows the current layout direction (LTR or RTL), detected automatically from the browser or system settings."],[262,"The shared structural containers composed together into a card-like layout. Each is a\nplain semantic region here; inside a parent that provides their contexts (e.g. \\`Modal\\`)\nthey adopt that parent's spacing automatically."],[1469,"The spacing props use semantic t-shirt sizes for padding, gap, and other spacing properties:"],[407,"The states **disabled**, **readonly**, and **invalid** are applied by the field wrapper (e.g. TextField, NumberField, Select). The group reflects them via data attributes on the group."],[75,"The tertiary button is the default, low-emphasis style used for common, non-critical actions."],[1226,"The Tooltip component displays a description of an element on hover or focus."],[1245,"The tooltip uses `role=\"tooltip\"` and is associated with its focusable element via `aria-describedby`."],[676,"The tooltip uses `role=\"tooltip\"` and is associated with the info trigger via `aria-describedby`."],[1023,"The track and thumb read from Antares curated tokens, falling back to legacy `--ux-*` custom properties:"],[296,"The whole field is a single focusable button; Enter/Space opens the popover"],[507,"These are re-exports of the underlying Bento Icon system methods. For complete API documentation, advanced usage patterns, and implementation details, see the `@bento/icon` and `@bento/svg-parser` package documentation."],[15,"This also works with autocomplete in IDEs and LLMs, so you can import from the root package and let your editor/agent suggest the available components."],[539,"This approach works well for SSR and small numbers of icons, but can lead to DOM bloat when the same icon appears many times."],[933,"Three sizes are available: \\`sm\\`, \\`md\